{
  "_comment": "Golden for finding (d), RFC 5545 section 3.6.1: an all-day event is DTSTART;VALUE=DATE with an EXCLUSIVE DTEND;VALUE=DATE (the day AFTER the last day). A stored event is all-day ONLY when (a) its start is a date-only string (YYYY-MM-DD; an end, if present, is date-only too), or (b) BOTH start and end are present, both are instants on the SAME boundary kind (both exactly T00:00:00Z, i.e. midnight UTC, or both exactly T22:00:00Z, i.e. midnight SAST), and end minus start is a whole number of days of at least 1. A start with no end, mixed boundary kinds, equal or reversed instants, or any non-boundary time is TIMED and is emitted exactly as before (DTSTART:...Z and, when an end exists, DTEND:...Z). The calendar date of a boundary value is its UTC date for T00:00:00Z and its SAST date (UTC date + 1) for T22:00:00Z; the end's calendar date is the LAST day, DTEND is that date plus one. Accepted residual ambiguity: a real timed event lasting exactly N whole days from one boundary to the same boundary (for example 02:00 SAST to 02:00 SAST the next day) is indistinguishable from an all-day range and is emitted as all-day; the proper fix is an explicit allDay field on the event later. Not fixtured: a date-only start with an instant end. Compared line by line with DTSTAMP removed. Line order: BEGIN, UID, DTSTART, DTEND, SUMMARY, DESCRIPTION, LOCATION, END.",
